# PIGNet2 as the authors pinned it, to settle one question: is the van der Waals discrepancy
# caused by torch_geometric?
#
# Everything else has been ruled out — checkpoint, model class, RDKit version, protonation,
# and the age of the golden file. What is left is that `GatedGAT` subclasses PyG's
# `MessagePassing`, which was rebuilt between 2.0 and 2.3, while the vdW term is the only
# energy that reads the node embeddings those convolutions produce.
#
# The conclusion recorded here was WRONG and is kept only so the correction travels with it.
# This image does reproduce the golden vdW of -2.074 where the other gives -3.518, but the two
# images differ in RDKit (2022.3.5 vs 2023.9.6), numpy and scipy as well as torch_geometric, so
# the comparison never isolated PyG. `probe_gatedgat.py` since ran GatedGAT under both PyG
# versions with fixed weights: attention logits, softmax, forward and the authors' own dense
# `compare()` all agree exactly. RDKit is the remaining candidate — node features depend on its
# bond and hybridisation perception, and vdW is the only energy reading node embeddings. The
# divergence is also complex-dependent (1a30 -2.865 vs -5.260, 1bzc -7.709 vs -7.697), which
# looks like perception on ambiguous molecules rather than changed arithmetic.
#
# NOTE: this file no longer builds. data.pyg.org has stopped serving torch-scatter wheels for
# torch 2.1.2, pip falls back to the sdist, and that build needs torch inside pip's isolated
# environment. The pignet2-ref image still exists locally; the recipe does not reproduce it.
#
# torch is 2.1.2 rather than the authors' 1.9.1, and only torch_geometric is pinned to their
# version. The experiment above isolates PyG as the cause, and torch 1.9.1 would force Python
# 3.9 — for which dimorphite-dl publishes nothing, leaving protonation off and the
# hydrogen-bond term at -0.743 instead of the golden's -1.021. Keeping torch 2.1.2 lets the
# vdW fix and the protonation fix hold at the same time, which neither older stack allows.
FROM docker.io/mambaorg/micromamba:1.5.8

USER root
ENV PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1 PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 MPLBACKEND=Agg
RUN micromamba install -y -n base -c conda-forge -c bioconda \
        python=3.10 pymol-open-source openbabel libstdcxx-ng reduce \
    && micromamba clean --all --yes
ENV PATH=/opt/conda/bin:${PATH}
ENV LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/conda/lib

RUN pip install --no-cache-dir torch==2.1.2 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu

RUN pip install --no-cache-dir \
        torch-scatter torch-sparse \
        -f https://data.pyg.org/whl/torch-2.1.2+cpu.html \
    && pip install --no-cache-dir "torch-geometric==2.0.3"

RUN pip install --no-cache-dir \
    "rdkit-pypi==2022.3.5" \
    "dimorphite-dl==1.2.5" \
    "biopython==1.79" \
    "hydra-core==1.2.0" \
    "omegaconf==2.2.2" \
    "numpy==1.22.4" \
    "scipy==1.7.2" \
    "pandas==1.4.3" \
    "scikit_learn==1.1.2" \
    "tqdm==4.64.0"

ENV PYTHONPATH=/work:/work/src:/work/src/exe:/work/dataset/preprocess

RUN python -c "import torch, torch_geometric, torch_scatter, rdkit, pymol; \
print('env ok', torch.__version__, torch_geometric.__version__)"

WORKDIR /work
COPY . /work
